A server for the small internet.

Version 1.0.0, released and signed. It has not been independently audited, and Agate and gmid have years of production hardening it does not.

Unseen Servant publishes one folder of writing to five small networks: Gemini, Gopher, Spartan, Nex and Finger, and mirrors it to the web. You write a page once. A reader opens it in Lagrange, in a gopher client from 1994, in lynx, or in Chrome, and it is the same page, from the same file, updated within seconds of you saving it.

The command is usv.

This site is that claim, tested on itself: everything you are reading is served by Unseen Servant, from one folder, on every protocol it supports, with no build step in between. If you are reading this over gopher or nex, that is the demonstration working.

